# BootLeft-1 (lane BootLeft, 2026-10-30): the solo DFlash2 drafter's CUDA graphs are captured only when something
# replays them (engine.solo_drafter_graphs). Their only replays are that drafter's own calls (the one-stream decode,
# drafter_choice, draft_dump, GlmEngine._calibrate); under --parallel every request runs through MultiDecoder, whose
# MultiDrafter has graphs of its own, and _calibrate runs there only without the batched windows' graphs. So they are
# captured whenever the one-stream graphs are (--parallel 1, TF_GLM_SOLO_GRAPHS=1, lone stream, profile, serial seam)
# or TF_GLM_MULTI_GRAPHS=0 (multi.batched_graphs, now the one reader of that variable), and not otherwise: production
# --parallel 2-8 skips 17 graphs (16 context-update sizes + the block pass), their eager runs' gathers and their
# private pool (64 MiB on the laptop rig). The decision joins the ranks' settings comparison. Replies unchanged.
--- tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/engine.py
